.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
\fBDrawing\fP attributes with programmed movement and appearance animation\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAnimatedAttributes\fP combines \fBAnimated\fP and \fBAttributes\fP\&. Construct it without a \fBDrawing\fP or \fBElementRef\fP; an optional \fBAttributes\fP argument seeds a snapshot of the initial values\&. Animation tracks are not copied\&. Call animate(deltaSeconds) once per update; MVC controllers already advance their Views\&. All durations, waits and update steps are floating-point seconds\&. It has no physics body and does not animate stored geometry\&.
.SH "Appearance channels"
.PP
The \fBchangeLineColor()\fP, \fBchangeLineThickness()\fP, \fBchangeLineOpacity()\fP, \fBchangeFillColor()\fP, \fBchangeFillOpacity()\fP, \fBchangeFillGradient()\fP, \fBchangeFillRadialGradient()\fP, \fBchangeRoundedCorners()\fP, \fBchangeTextSize()\fP, \fBchangeSubsection()\fP, \fBchangeSphereRotation()\fP, \fBchangePolarOffset()\fP, \fBchangeLightOffset()\fP and \fBchangeAmbientLight()\fP methods take their target values, an explicit duration in seconds and an optional easing constant (linearTween by default)\&. Sphere rotation also accepts an integer rotationDirection constant after easing\&.

.PP
blendMode, font, clipOverflow, lineStyle, textStyle, texture and fitType only have immediate setters\&. No texture crossfade or interpolation of enum values is implied\&. Gradient modes switch discretely when their delay expires; their numeric/color values interpolate\&. Choosing a solid, linear or radial fill interrupts all previous fill-color/gradient tracks, but leaves fill opacity and other channels alone\&. Line/fill methods resolve lineStyle_Auto when requested, as \fBAttributes\fP does\&.

.PP
changeFrames(first, last, seconds, easing) visits an inclusive sequence of integer frames in either direction, with equal time per frame before easing\&. It holds the last frame at completion\&. A wait preserves the previous frame until the sequence starts\&. Direct \fBframe()\fP calls interrupt the sequence\&.

.PP
Immediate setters interrupt their matching tracks\&. Independent channels continue\&. wait(seconds) delays the next timed request, which begins from the value at the end of the delay\&. Retargeting replaces a channel's pending request\&. \fBDrawing\fP and \fBElementRef\fP copy \fBAttributes\fP by default; use \fBElementRef::setLiveAttributes()\fP to follow subsequent samples\&.
.SH "Transform model"
.PP
The initial logical size is 1 by 1, independent of \fBDrawing\fP geometry\&. Separate x/y transform scale defaults to (1,1); scaling leaves logical size unchanged\&. \fBAnimated\fP movement, rotation, size and scale share one affine transform with the appearance attributes\&. Its composition is translation, pivot, rotation, shear, logical size, independent scale, inverse-pivot\&. The inherited \fBAttributes\fP methods \fBtranslation()\fP, \fBrotation()\fP, \fBscale()\fP, \fBskew()\fP and \fBtransform()\fP postmultiply the current matrix; \fBsetTransform()\fP replaces it\&. Matrix edits and matrix tweens preserve logical width and height and update \fBAnimated\fP position, rotation and independent scale\&. Shear and singular matrices are retained\&. For example, setScale(2) followed by scale(3) leaves \fBgetScale()\fP at (6,6), without changing logical size\&. \fBgrow()\fP and \fBstretch()\fP change logical size while preserving scale\&.

.PP
Use the inherited \fBAnimated\fP methods for position, rotation, size and scale: \fBmoveTo()\fP sets an absolute location, \fBrotateTo()\fP sets an absolute angle with optional rotation direction, \fBresizeTo()\fP sets logical width/height, and \fBchangeScaleTo()\fP sets independent x/y scale\&. \fBmoveBy()\fP, \fBrotateBy()\fP, \fBresizeBy()\fP, \fBgrow()\fP and \fBstretch()\fP make relative changes\&. Their timed overloads use easeInOutQuad by default; pass linearTween explicitly for constant interpolation\&. \fBsetLocation()\fP, \fBsetRotation()\fP, \fBsetSize()\fP and \fBsetScale()\fP apply immediate changes\&. Programmed movement, spin and growth update the same matrix on each \fBanimate()\fP step\&. These changes are visible through \fBgetTransform()\fP and in \fBAttributes\fP snapshots passed to \fBDrawing\fP\&. A component request interrupts a whole-matrix tween at its current sample\&. \fBchangeSkew()\fP postmultiplies a shear onto the current matrix and interpolates to that result\&. \fBchangeTransform()\fP replaces the matrix by interpolating its six affine coefficients\&. Such interpolation can pass through a singular matrix and does not select an angular route: use \fBrotateBy()\fP/rotateTo() for rotations\&. Matrices use column-major arrays of nine numbers in JavaScript and glm::mat3 in C++\&.

.PP
The \fBAttributes\fP composition calls are immediate drawing-transform operations\&. \fBtranslation()\fP adds an offset along the current transformed axes; \fBrotation()\fP adds a rotation around the supplied local center; \fBscale()\fP multiplies the current transform around its supplied center\&. \fBsetLocation()\fP, \fBrotateTo()\fP and \fBchangeScaleTo()\fP instead target individual \fBAnimated\fP components\&. Both APIs keep the same matrix and \fBAnimated\fP state synchronized\&. Composition replaces transform tracks and stops programmed transform rates at the current sample\&. Like other immediate edits, \fBtranslation()\fP, \fBrotation()\fP and \fBscale()\fP reject a pending \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP\&.

.PP
Translation and axis scaling preserve existing rotation, signed scale and shear; axis scaling multiplies the independent scale directly, even on collapsed axes\&. General affine edits decompose matrix column lengths into independent scale relative to the existing logical dimensions\&. A zero logical dimension can only represent a zero corresponding matrix column; an incompatible matrix request throws instead of changing that dimension\&. A queued matrix request is checked again when it starts, after any preceding resize\&.
.SH "Language and Drawing integration"
.PP
In C++, this class publicly derives from both \fBAnimated\fP and \fBAttributes\fP, so it can be passed as either base reference\&. In JavaScript it inherits from \fBAnimated\fP and exposes the complete \fBAttributes\fP method surface\&. It is instanceof \fBAnimated\fP and instanceof \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP, but not instanceof \fBAttributes\fP; native \fBAttributes\fP arguments in \fBPort\fP, \fBDrawing\fP and \fBElementRef\fP accept it with the correct base-pointer conversion\&. Copies of \fBAttributes\fP contain values, without animation tracks\&.

.PP
Views derive from \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP\&. Their size remains the layout rectangle's width and height, and their location is its center\&. Passing a View directly as \fBAttributes\fP therefore maps centered unit coordinates onto the view rectangle\&. Existing ControlAttributes themes remain separate; inheriting this class does not automatically replace every themed drawing primitive's attributes\&. General MVC clipping/hit-testing for rotation and reflection remains pending\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const style = new pdg\&.AnimatedAttributes();
style\&.fillColor(new pdg\&.Color(1, 0, 0));
style\&.changeFillColor(new pdg\&.Color(0, 0, 1), 0\&.5, pdg\&.easeInOutQuad);
style\&.changeFillOpacity(0\&.25, 0\&.5);
style\&.animate(0\&.25);
// This Drawing element captures the current sample; it is not a live association\&.
const drawing = pdg\&.createDrawing();
const element = drawing\&.addRect(new pdg\&.Rect(0, 0, 100, 40), style);
// Explicitly applying a later sample remains possible:
style\&.animate(0\&.25);
element\&.setAttributes(style);
.fi
.PP
 
