.SS "\fBAnimatedAttributes\fP changeFillColor (\fBColor\fP target, number seconds, int easing = \fR\fBlinearTween\fP\fP)"

.PP
Animate solid fill color\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Replaces the matching pending transition and consumes the pending wait\&. The immediate \fBfillColor()\fP setter interrupts this channel; unrelated channels continue\&. Selects a solid fill and replaces previous solid/gradient fill-color tracks\&. Fill opacity remains independent\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP Target \fBColor\fP, interpolated component by component\&. 
.br
\fIseconds\fP Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds\&. Zero applies the target immediately\&. After \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP, duration must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Integer easing constant, such as \fR\fBpdg\&.linearTween\fP\fP or \fR\fBpdg\&.easeInOutQuad\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Advance a standalone object with animate(deltaSeconds)\&. \fBDrawing\fP and \fBElementRef\fP copy a sample of \fBAttributes\fP; use \fBElementRef\&.setLiveAttributes()\fP to follow later samples\&. MVC controllers advance their Views automatically\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const style = new pdg\&.AnimatedAttributes();
style\&.fillColor(new pdg\&.Color(1, 0, 0));
style\&.changeFillColor(new pdg\&.Color(0, 0, 1), 0\&.5);
style\&.animate(0\&.25);
const drawing = pdg\&.createDrawing();
const element = drawing\&.addRect(new pdg\&.Rect(0, 0, 20, 10), style);
style\&.animate(0\&.25);
element\&.setAttributes(style);

.fi
.PP
.RE
