.SS "\fBAnimatedAttributes\fP changeFrames (int first, int last, number seconds, int easing = \fR\fBlinearTween\fP\fP)"

.PP
Animate an inclusive sequence of image frames\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Visits first through last in either direction, with equal time per frame before easing\&. Does not loop; holds the last frame at completion\&. A pending wait keeps the old frame until the sequence starts\&. Calling \fBframe()\fP directly cancels the sequence\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfirst\fP First integer frame index\&. 
.br
\fIlast\fP Last integer frame index, inclusive\&. 
.br
\fIseconds\fP Finite nonnegative duration of the entire sequence, in seconds\&. Zero selects the last frame when the delay expires\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Integer easing constant, such as \fR\fBpdg\&.linearTween\fP\fP or \fR\fBpdg\&.easeInOutQuad\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
style\&.changeFrames(0, 7, 0\&.8);
// Call style\&.animate(deltaSeconds) and reapply it each update\&.

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBframe()\fP, \fBAnimated::wait()\fP 
.RE
.PP

