.SS "\fBAnimatedAttributes\fP changeTransform (array number matrix, number seconds, int easing = \fR\fBlinearTween\fP\fP)"

.PP
Animate a replacement affine matrix\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fReasing:\fP \fBEasingFunction\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Interpolates the six affine coefficients, which may pass through singular matrices\&. Preserves logical width and height; matrix scale updates the independent scale components\&. A nonzero matrix column requires a nonzero corresponding logical dimension\&. Use \fBrotateTo()\fP for angular paths and direction control\&. Replaces transform tracks and constant transform rates; subsequent component requests interrupt the matrix tween at its current sample\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImatrix\fP Column-major array of nine finite numbers: [a, b, 0, c, d, 0, tx, ty, 1]\&. It maps (x,y) to (a*x+c*y+tx, b*x+d*y+ty)\&. 
.br
\fIseconds\fP Required finite, nonnegative duration in seconds\&. Zero applies the target immediately\&. After \fBwait()\fP or \fBandThen()\fP, duration must be greater than zero\&. 
.br
\fIeasing\fP Integer easing constant, such as \fR\fBpdg\&.linearTween\fP\fP or \fR\fBpdg\&.easeInOutQuad\fP\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
style\&.changeTransform([1, 0, 0, 0\&.25, 1, 0, 30, 10, 1], 0\&.5);

.fi
.PP
.RE
